    {
      "id": "b00cc2fec158657074e10ce6423eeaeb94505814",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 681316873,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Just out of interest, is there a use case for actually displaying (the very verbose on Linux) locale?\n\nChange e015eca944700064f4ea0e8dab4dcd17e3e87be2:\n\n```\ncommit e015eca944700064f4ea0e8dab4dcd17e3e87be2\nAuthor: Stig Bjørlykke <stig@bjorlykke.org>\nDate:   Wed Jun 29 08:05:53 2011 +0000\n\n    Show locale in version info (if !win32).\n    This may help us identifying bugs related to locale.\n    \n    svn path=/trunk/; revision=37829\n```\n\nintroduced the locale to the version info; it just read the `LANG` environment variable on UN\\*X and reported that.\n\nChange 9a7d4559aed27208b4688cb6d0c9c8a810612788:\n\n```\ncommit 9a7d4559aed27208b4688cb6d0c9c8a810612788\nAuthor: Guy Harris <guy@alum.mit.edu>\nDate:   Wed Dec 31 15:32:42 2014 -0800\n\n    Use setlocale() to get the current locale.\n    \n    This:\n    \n            1) should work on Windows;\n    \n            2) reflects what the C environment is actually set up to use,\n               rather than what the environment variables for locale are\n               set up to use - C programs default to the C locale and only\n               pick up the setting from the environment variables etc. if\n               you explicitly request the system locale with a setlocale()\n               call.\n\n    Change-Id: Iee064237e70501a5450d4daa9ab849391f200efd\n    Reviewed-on: https://code.wireshark.org/review/6195\n    Reviewed-by: Guy Harris <guy@alum.mit.edu>\n```\n\nchanged it to print what `setlocale()` reports, which may not be simplified if all the components of the locale are the same, rather than just printing `LANG`.\n\nChange c18736c2e7f9e56fa61658d6b4f8c172fc53f2bd:\n\n```\ncommit c18736c2e7f9e56fa61658d6b4f8c172fc53f2bd\nAuthor: João Valverde <j@v6e.pt>\nDate:   Sat Mar 12 15:59:10 2016 +0000\n\n    wsutil: Split locale information into tokens and format it\n    \n    The locale information returned by setlocale() can be a very long unbroken\n    string. This makes the text dialog too wide without line wrapping and in\n    some cases it spans outside the screen border.\n    \n    Add some commas to improve readability and help GTK+ render it properly.\n    \n    Change-Id: Ia7913550ada3ebaac9c783e9ac1b202dbe1563fc\n    Reviewed-on: https://code.wireshark.org/review/11961\n    Petri-Dish: Alexis La Goutte <alexis.lagoutte@gmail.com>\n    Tested-by: Petri Dish Buildbot <buildbot-no-reply@wireshark.org>\n    Reviewed-by: Anders Broman <a.broman58@gmail.com>\n```\n\nchanged it to report the locale information more cleanly.\n\nPerhaps having it check to see if *all* the settings are LC_xxx=YYY, where YYY is the same for all of them, and just reporting LANG=YYY if so, would mean that it's typically less messy.\n\nAnd, frankly, if the goal is to produce output that helps determine what's going on in a bug report, what might be useful is a \"dump status information to a file\" routines that reports all that *plus* the settings of all preferences *plus* the enabled/disabled statuses of all dissectors *plus* all of the dissector tables, so that the user can attach that to a bug report.\n\nThen we could decide which information is useful to people *not* submitting bug reports, and put that in the version dialog, etc..",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-18T22:56:20.547Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-18T22:56:20.547Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 117415099,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4230,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5f25586c32c9bf9b15237d9436072dc8a317dad8",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 681317799,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I agree with using `setlocale()` because it is the canonical source of truth, `LANG` is just a default, but we should probably include just LC_CTYPE.\n\n>>>\nAnd, frankly, if the goal is to produce output that helps determine what's going on in a bug report, what might be useful is a \"dump status information to a file\" routines that reports all that *plus* the settings of all preferences *plus* the enabled/disabled statuses of all dissectors *plus* all of the dissector tables, so that the user can attach that to a bug report.\n>>>\n\nThis too. We should have separate routines for show_version() and dump_bug_report_information().",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-18T23:02:55.709Z",
